What this software does with your data

SocialMCP reads the data export you give it and stores the result in a single
SQLite file on the computer it runs on. It collects no analytics, sends no
telemetry, and has no account, server or sign-in of any kind. It never logs in
to any social network, never uses a password or session cookie, and never reads
any website.

The only outbound network request it can make is to an embedding provider you
configure yourself, which defaults to a model running on your own machine
(127.0.0.1:11434) and can be switched off entirely.

Deleting the database file deletes everything it holds.

